Package: aurora-fido
Architecture: arm64
Depends: aurora-sep, python3, python3-cryptography, systemd, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Suggests: libnotify-bin, fido2-tools, libpam-u2f, python3-jeepney
Description: Touch ID as a FIDO2/U2F security key
 aurora-fido makes this Mac's Secure Enclave and Touch ID a FIDO2/U2F
 security key: a uhid device that browsers (WebAuthn), OpenSSH (ecdsa-sk)
 and pam_u2f use like any USB key. Its keys live in the Secure Enclave,
 which checks the Touch ID match inside each signature.
 .
 It is opt in and installed off: "sudo aurora-fido enable" turns it on.
 python3-jeepney is needed for the per-user passkey agent (vault = user),
 libnotify-bin for the "Touch ID to sign in" notification.
